    {
      "id": "process-invalidated-outputs",
      "name": "ProcessInvalidatedOutputs",
      "category": "MovieSceneOverlappingEntityTracker",
      "signature": "ProcessInvalidatedOutputs<HandlerType>(Target, Linker, In Handler)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TOverlappingEntityTrackerImpl*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Linker",
          "type": "UMovieSceneEntitySystemLinker*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Handler",
          "type": "HandlerType&&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<HandlerType> void",
      "docs": "Process any outputs that were invalidated as a result of Update being called using a custom handler.\nInHandler    Any user-defined handler type that contains the following named functions:\n// Called when an output is first created\nvoid InitializeOutput(InputKeyTypes... Inputs, TArrayView<const FMovieSceneEntityID> Inputs, OutputType* Output, FEntityOutputAggregate Aggregate);\n// Called when an output has been updated with new inputs\nvoid UpdateOutput(InputKeyTypes... Inputs, TArrayView<const FMovieSceneEntityID> Inputs, OutputType* Output, FEntityOutputAggregate Aggregate);\n// Called when all an output's inputs are no longer relevant, and as such the output should be destroyed (or restored)\nvoid DestroyOutput(InputKeyTypes... Inputs, OutputType* Output, FEntityOutputAggregate Aggregate);"
    },
